    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 20a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.18"/> he heorðfæst, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.18"/> he folgere, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.18"/> on hundrede ⁊ on borge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.19"/> gebroht, ⁊ gehealde se borh hine ⁊ gelæde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.20"/> to ælcan rihte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Sy he heorðfæst, sy hé folgere, <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.4"/>þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc sy on hundre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.5"/> ⁊ on borh gebroht, ⁊ gehealde se borh híne ⁊ gelæde to ælcon gerihte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="322" ed="#liebermann"/>Sy he heorþfæst, sy he folgere, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc sy on hundrede ⁊ on borge gebroht, ⁊ gehealde se borh hine ⁊ læde to ælce rihte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Sit heorðfest<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.7"/>, sit folgarius: sit in hundreto et plegio constitutus, et teneat eum plegius et adducat ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.8"/> omne rectum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Hoc quoque dicimus et de iis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.14"/> qui domum et terram habent et de iis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.15"/> qui non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.16"/>, sed seruiunt aliis, quos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.17"/> Angli uocant husfæst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.18-2"/> ⁊ folgæres, ut omnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.7-2"/> sint in hundredo et sub plegio, qui eos (teneat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.19-2"/>) ad iusticiam habeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.20-2"/>, si aliquando calumniantur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.21"/> de aliqua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.oe.22"/> re.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20a" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Siue paterfamilias siue cliens (sit, uolumus), ut omnis sit in centenario et fideiussione positus, et fideiussor eum seruet et ad omnem rectitudinem perducat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20[b]" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>sy he heorðfæst, sy hé folgere—þæt ælc sy on hundre[d]<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_20a.robnote.fn.5"/> ⁊ on borh<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_20a.robnote.fn.6"/> gebroht ⁊ gehealde se borh híne ⁊ gelæde to ælcon gerihte<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_20a.robnote.fn.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Si he heorðfæst, si he folgere, þæt ælc si on hundrede and on borge gebroht, and gehealde se borh hine and gelæde to ælcan rihte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="323" ed="#liebermann"/>Sei er hausangesessen, sei er [Miteinwohner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.de.1"/> vom Haushalts]gefolge: jeder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_20a.lnote.de.2"/> werde in Hundertschaft und in Bürgschaft gebracht; und dieser Bürge[nverband?] halte ihn [in Aufsicht] und stelle ihn zu jeder Rechtspflicht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whether he be a householder or a [household] follower: let each be brought into a hundred and under surety, and let the surety keep him and bring him to every legal obligation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>whether he has an establishment of his own or is in the service of another—everyone shall be brought within a hundred and under surety, and his surety shall hold and bring him to the performance of every legal duty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>Whether he has a home of his own, or is in the following of another, each is to be brought into a hundred and under surety, and the surety is to hold him and bring him to every legal duty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Whether independent or in service, everyone is to be enrolled in a hundred and under a surety, and that surety shall maintain him and guide him in his legal obligations.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="323"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_6">III Eg 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Eg. 6</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_25">Leis Wl 25</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_6">III Eg 6</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 20a: III Eg 6</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Eg 6.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 323, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">surety: In other words, each free person is to have someone to guarantee that they will fulfill their obligations to the court and the community.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit, u. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit, u. lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingeschoben</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> hundred</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read hundred</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rdf. <hi rend="italic">Dm;</hi> heohd'f. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> -fast <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rdf. Dm; heohd'f. K; -fast Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt KDm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in KDm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_20a.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">322</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">borghe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">borghe Ld</seg></note>
